00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.269 align:start position:0%
felipe torres and his family fled their  modest farm in the rural area of the  border city of cucuta four months ago  when a group of 100 armed men set camp  there  after felipe asked them to leave he says  he received threats and then was shot  four times  i just asked them to move away from the  house not the entire farm or the area  because as i told them if you are here  it's because the army allows you to  instead one of theirs was killed and  then they came after me  thousands of colombian farmers were  displaced from the northeastern  countryside surrounding kukuta last year  as a paramilitary group entered the area  fighting with communist eln rebels  they're battling for control of cocaine  production and the contraband routes  along the border with venezuela  during the last 20 months 22 community  leaders have been killed in north of  santondo region  in the last 45 days  20 leaders 14 of them women have been  displaced this is a true humanitarian  disaster in the past the city of cucuta  was mostly spared the worst of the  conflict that affected remote parts of  this region but things have changed  in june a car bomb exploded in the  city's military base injuring 36 people  a week later gunfire hit a helicopter  carrying colombian president ivan duque  as it took off  at the beginning of october president  duke announced the deployment of a new  military unit of 14 000 soldiers to  address the situation  but three weeks after the announcement  locals say nothing has changed in their  communities we repeatedly asked the new  units commander for an interview but so  far they've said they have nothing new  to add  local officials say increasing troops on  the ground alone will not solve a  situation that requires real  alternatives for poor coca farmers and  that a lack of diplomatic relations  between colombia and venezuela  facilitated the expansion of criminal  groups to the city  la dynamica de los ultimos anos  the border dynamic of the last few years  with the closures and the lack of  communication between the states has  facilitated the growth of these criminal  activities offering them the best  possible environment for their eyes  an explosive cocktail that leaves people  like felipe wondering if they will ever  be able to get their life back  alessandra  al jazeera
 

